==Old English==

===Etymology===
Germanic ''*falwo-, falwa-'', from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|pel-|lang=ine-pro}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon [[falu]] (Dutch [[vaal]]), Old High German [[falo]] (German [[fahl]]), Old Norse [[fǫlr]].  The common Germanic is cognate with Latin [[pallidus]], Ancient Greek [[πελιτνός]] and Old Armenian {{term|ալիք||wave, gray hair|tr=alikʿ|lang=xcl}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfæalu/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
'''fealu'''

# [[yellow]], [[dusky]], [[grey]]

